{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "HV600 HVAC fan and pump drive (MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "hv600",
  "short_model": "HV600",
  "aliases": [
    "CIPR-HV60",
    "HV600 HVAC drive"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa HV600 drives using the built-in RS-485 port with H5-08 = 0 (MEMOBUS/Modbus), per technical reference SIEPC71061732 revision F.",
  "summary": "Yaskawa's HVAC fan and pump variable frequency drive. Its built-in RS-485 port speaks MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU, Metasys N2, Apogee P1 or BACnet MS/TP, selected by H5-08. Commands go to hex registers 0001H-000FH, status, faults and monitors are read from 0020H onwards, and each parameter has its own hex register. This map covers the command block, status and fault words, the key monitors with fixed units and the b1/H5 communication parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 31,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Register numbers are hex and are sent unchanged: the manual's read example asks for starting register 0020H as 00 20. Parameters use the hex number printed under each parameter (H5-01 = 0425H)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "HV600 AC Drive Technical Reference",
    "doc_number": "SIEPC71061732F",
    "revision_date": "2024-02",
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPC71061732&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPC71061732.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 6.6 MEMOBUS/Modbus: Table 6.22 function codes, Enter command p. 307, Table 6.32 command data pp. 309-310, Table 6.33 monitor data pp. 314-317; H5 parameters pp. 558-559 and chapter 12"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Frequency registers 0002H, 0023H and 0024H use the units chosen in o1-03, so they are left unscaled.",
    "Left out: 0025H output voltage (unit switched by H5-10), 0026H output current (0.1 A in Table 6.33, but U1-03 resolution can depend on drive capacity), 0027H output power and 0028H/0032H torque reference (units/sign not fixed in the table), 002FH frequency reference bias, 0034H/0035H product codes, 003EH/003FH output frequency in r/min and % (sign not stated), and the long fault-history and U-monitor blocks from 0040H.",
    "b1-01/b1-02 value 2 is called Serial Communications on this drive; it covers whichever protocol H5-08 selects. b1-02 settings 7-9 are the HOA AUTO modes.",
    "Supported function codes are 03H, 08H, 10H, 5AH and 67H (non-consecutive read/write); there is no 06H, so use 10H even for a single register. A 03H read returns at most 16 registers.",
    "With H5-11 = 0 parameter writes only take effect after writing 0 to 0900H (EEPROM) or 0910H (RAM). Command registers 0001H-000FH never need Enter. Reading 0900H/0910H returns error 02H."
  ],
